/target
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is deliberately committed. This crate is not consumed as a Rust library; it is a
# cdylib compiled into a binary that ships inside the NuGet package. An unpinned dependency graph
# would make the build non-reproducible, and `cargo build --locked` cannot create a lockfile it
# does not find.
pkg/
wasm-pack.log
node_modules
/build/*/**
!/build/*/package.json
.env
.Net/OPAQUE.Net/.vs
.Net/OPAQUE.Net/obj
.Net/OPAQUE.Net/bin
.Net/Test/obj
bin
target
# Auditorias de segurança (nunca versionar)
/security-audit/
# Native libraries are build products: CI builds them from src/ and Cargo.lock and publish.yaml
# packs those. They are never committed (a stale committed binary once shipped pre-hardening code).
/.Net/OPAQUE.Net/*.so
/.Net/OPAQUE.Net/*.dll
/.Net/OPAQUE.Net/*.dylib
